   "notes": [
    "1. A short from an output to VCC+ overheats the part and may destroy it. Output current limits at about 20 mA whatever VCC+ is.",
    "2. Shorts heat the part; all four outputs shorted together can dissipate enough to destroy it. The thermal resistances are typical figures.",
    "3. HBM: 100 pF charged to the rated voltage and discharged through 1.5 kΩ between each pair of connected pins, the rest left open.",
    "4. MM: 200 pF charged to the rated voltage and discharged straight between each pair of connected pins, no series resistor (under 5 Ω inside), the rest left open.",
    "5. CDM: every pin and the package charged together to the rated voltage, then discharged to ground through a single pin, repeated for each pin.",
    "Rthjc unit should read °C/W."
   ]
