   "notes": [
    "1. Taken where the output switches, VO ≈ 1.4 V, with RS = 0, for VCC+ anywhere from 5 V to 30 V over the full common-mode span (0 V up to 1.5 V below VCC+).",
    "2. The PNP input stage makes the input current flow out of the pins. It stays nearly the same in either output state, so it puts no changing load on the reference or input lines.",
    "3. Measured with a 100 mV step at the input, overdriving the threshold by 5 mV.",
    "4. Either input may rise above the supply; if the second input remains inside its common-mode span, the output still reads correctly. An input must not go lower than –0.3 V, or 0.3 V under the negative supply where one is used.",
    "5. Maxima are set by design rather than tested.",
    "Note marker (3) should sit on tres and (4) on Vid."
