   "title": "Figure 21. Two-decade high-frequency VCO",
   "page": 8,
   "description": "A two-decade high-frequency VCO from three sections on VCC+ = +30 V. Vcontrol feeds the first section's inverting input through 100 kΩ and its non-inverting input through 20 kΩ (20 kΩ to ground); 10 kΩ and 0.1 µF in series join the two inputs, and 500 pF runs from the inverting input to the output, which is Output 2 (triangle) with 3 kΩ to VCC+ and 0.01 µF to ground. The second section takes that through 5.1 kΩ to its non-inverting input, with 100 kΩ from its output and its inverting input at VCC+/2; its output, with 3 kΩ to VCC+, is Output 1 (square) and drives the third section's non-inverting input. The third section, inverting input at VCC+/2, drives the 50 kΩ resistor to the first section's inverting input.",
